 {
  "title": "Chilli Con Carne with Red Lentils & Kidney Beans",
  "servings": "4",
  "time": "15 min prep + 6–8 hr (low)",
  "intro": "A proper slow-cooked chilli. Red lentils melt into the sauce and make it thick and rich. Roughly 40–42 g protein per serve.",
  "sections": [
   {
    "kind": "ingredients",
    "heading": "Ingredients",
    "items": [
     {
      "text": "500 g lean beef mince"
     },
     {
      "text": "1 onion, diced"
     },
     {
      "text": "1 capsicum, diced"
     },
     {
      "text": "3 garlic cloves, crushed"
     },
     {
      "text": "2 tsp chilli powder (or to taste)"
     },
     {
      "text": "2 tsp ground cumin"
     },
     {
      "text": "1 tsp smoked paprika"
     },
     {
      "text": "1 tsp dried oregano"
     },
     {
      "text": "½ cup dry red lentils, rinsed"
     },
     {
      "text": "2 cans kidney beans, drained and rinsed"
     },
     {
      "text": "1 can crushed tomatoes"
     },
     {
      "text": "2 tbsp tomato paste"
     },
     {
      "text": "1 cup beef stock"
     },
     {
      "text": "1 tsp cocoa powder (optional — adds depth)"
     },
     {
      "text": "Salt and pepper"
     },
     {
      "group": "To serve"
     },
     {
      "text": "Rice or baked potatoes, Greek yoghurt, grated cheese, coriander"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "kind": "steps",
    "heading": "Method",
    "items": [
     {
      "text": "**Brown the mince.** In a frying pan, brown the mince with the onion and capsicum. Add the garlic and spices for the last minute."
     },
     {
      "text": "**Load the slow cooker.** Tip into the slow cooker and stir in the lentils, beans, tomatoes, tomato paste, stock and cocoa."
     },
     {
      "text": "**Slow cook.** Cook on Low for 6–8 hours (or High for 3–4)."
     },
     {
      "text": "Season to taste, loosen with a splash of water if needed, and serve with rice or potatoes and toppings."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "kind": "notes",
    "heading": "Notes",
    "items": [
     {
      "text": "Freezes brilliantly — portion leftovers for nachos, jacket potatoes or burritos."
     },
     {
      "text": "For a quicker version, see Beef & Vegetable Chilli (Stovetop) or Beef & Mixed Bean Chilli (Instant Pot)."
     }
    ]
   }
  ],
