 {
  "title": "Banana Bread",
  "servings": "1 loaf (10 slices)",
  "time": "1 hr 15 min",
  "intro": "",
  "sections": [
   {
    "kind": "ingredients",
    "heading": "Ingredients",
    "items": [
     {
      "text": "3 very ripe bananas, mashed (about 1¼ cups)"
     },
     {
      "text": "75 g butter, melted"
     },
     {
      "text": "¾ cup brown sugar"
     },
     {
      "text": "1 egg"
     },
     {
      "text": "1 tsp vanilla essence"
     },
     {
      "text": "1 tsp baking soda"
     },
     {
      "text": "Pinch of salt"
     },
     {
      "text": "1½ cups plain flour"
     },
     {
      "text": "½ cup chocolate chips or chopped walnuts (optional)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "kind": "steps",
    "heading": "Method",
    "items": [
     {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 175°C bake. Grease and line a loaf tin (about 22 × 12cm)."
     },
     {
      "text": "Mix the mashed banana and melted butter in a large bowl."
     },
     {
      "text": "Stir in the brown sugar, egg and vanilla."
     },
     {
      "text": "Sprinkle over the baking soda and salt, then add the flour and fold until just combined. Fold in the chocolate chips or walnuts, if using."
     },
     {
      "text": "Pour into the tin and bake for 55–65 minutes, until a skewer in the centre comes out clean. Cover loosely with foil for the last 15 minutes if it's browning too fast."
     },
     {
      "text": "Cool in the tin for 10 minutes, then turn out onto a wire rack."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "kind": "notes",
    "heading": "Notes",
    "items": [
     {
      "text": "In line with Chelsea's one-bowl banana loaf. The spottier the bananas, the sweeter and moister the loaf. Freeze overripe bananas in their skins and thaw them for this. Slices freeze well — toast them straight from frozen."
     }
    ]
   }
  ],
